"""Micras wall sensor: an SFH 4550 IR LED stacked over a TPS601A phototransistor, through-hole.

A custom part: the two leaded devices, bare (no casing), have their leads bent
90 degrees so they lie flat and look forward, the LED (pads 1-2) above the
phototransistor (pads 3-4). Pads from the Altium MicrasLib; bodies from the
datasheet outlines below.

Mechanics, in the footprint frame (the sensor looks along -y; heights above the
board top). The STEP (WALL_SENSOR_STACKED) draws both parts at nominal size; it
is MicrasHardware micras/leds.py sensor_model(), built from these numbers:
| | SFH 4550 (SFH-DS p.10) | TPS601A(F) (TPS-DS p.1, package 0-5A1) |
|---|---|---|
| optical axis height | 9.75 mm | 3.25 mm |
| seating plane (flange back) | y = 2.32 | y = 0.445 |
| flange | 5.5-5.9 dia, cathode flat | 5.8 dia max, 0.5 +/- 0.2 thick, key tab 1.0 x 1.0 |
| body | 4.8-5.1 dia, hemispherical lens | can 4.7 +0.1/-0.15 dia, 4.5 +/- 0.3 high, lens |
| seating plane to lens tip | 8.2-9.0 (tip y = -6.28 nominal) | 6.5 +/- 0.5 (tip y = -6.055 nominal) |
| leads | 0.4-0.6 square, bent 2.55 behind the body | 0.45 +/- 0.1 round, bent 2.0 behind the body |
The TPS601A leads are formed at the 2 mm minimum of TPS-DS p.2 (Precaution 2);
the SFH 4550 datasheet sets no forming distance. The courtyard (F.CrtYd) is
both bodies at their largest plus the pads, with 0.25 mm excess (IPC-7351B);
the silkscreen outlines the bodies 0.15 mm outside their largest outline and
the lead area behind them; User.13 draws the bodies at nominal size.

Pins (pad = symbol pin):
| Pad | Pin | Device |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | LED_A | SFH 4550 anode |
| 2 | LED_K | SFH 4550 cathode (the package's marked lead, SFH-DS p.10) |
| 3 | PT_C | TPS601A collector (pin 2 of the TPS601A) |
| 4 | PT_E | TPS601A emitter (pin 1 of the TPS601A) |

The footprint's pad numbers are not the manufacturers' lead numbers: the SFH
4550 recommended solder pad calls the cathode "Pad 1" (SFH-DS p.11), and the
TPS601A numbers its emitter 1 and collector 2 (TPS-DS p.1, "Pin Connection").
Fit each lead to the pad named above.

SFH 4550, 850 nm IR emitter, radial T1 3/4 (ams-OSRAM SFH 4550 datasheet
Version 1.9, 2022-08-09, "SFH-DS"):
- Maximum ratings (p.4): IF 100 mA DC; IF pulse 1 A at tp <= 400 us, D <= 0.005;
  VR 5 V; Ptot 180 mW; Tj 100 C; -40 to +100 C operating.
- Characteristics (p.5): VF 1.5 V typ, 1.7 V max at 100 mA (tp = 20 ms);
  2.4 V typ, 2.9 V max at 1 A (tp = 100 us); half angle +/-3 deg;
  tr = tf = 12 ns; RthJA 450 K/W.
- Pulse handling: the "Permissible Pulse Handling Capability" charts give the
  allowed pulse current against tp with the duty cycle D as parameter (read from
  Version 1.8, 2021-11-18, p.6: OHF05438 at TA = 25 C, OHF05587 at 85 C; the
  v1.9 copy of the page was not retrieved). At tp = 150 us: 0.59 A at D = 0.1
  and 0.38 A at D = 0.2 (25 C); about 0.12 A and 0.07 A (85 C). The DC limit on
  the same page falls linearly from 100 mA at 25 C to 0 at 100 C (OHR00880).
  `emitter_pulse_current` is the D = 0.2 point at 25 C, the conservative bound
  for any duty up to 0.2 and any tp up to 150 us (the curves fall with both).
  Inference, not a datasheet value: the 85 C points are the 25 C ones scaled by
  (100 C - TA) / 75 K, so a pulse current I at D = 0.2 holds up to about
  TA = 100 C - 75 K x I / 0.38 A.

TPS601A(F), NPN phototransistor, TO-18 metal can (Toshiba TPS601A(F) datasheet,
2004-02-06, "TPS-DS"):
- Maximum ratings (p.1): VCEO 40 V, VECO 5 V, IC 50 mA, PC 150 mW
  (-1.2 mW/C above 25 C), -40 to +125 C operating.
- Characteristics (p.2): light current IL at VCE = 3 V, E = 0.1 mW/cm2:
  100 uA min (no rank), A 100-300 uA, B 200-600 uA, C 400-1200 uA;
  VCE(sat) 0.4 V max at IC = 30 uA; tr = tf = 2 us typ at VCC = 5 V,
  IC = 10 mA, RL = 100 ohm; peak sensitivity 800 nm; half angle +/-10 deg.
- Curves (p3-4, typ, read): IL-E about 0.26 mA at 0.1 mW/cm2 and 4 mA at
  1 mW/cm2 (2870 K, IL grows as E^1.2); spectral response 9 % at 500 nm,
  47 % at 600 nm, 87 % at 700 nm, 100 % at 800 nm, 92 % at 850 nm, 25 % at
  1000 nm, 1.5 % at 1100 nm; directional sensitivity near zero beyond 20 deg.
  The unranked TPS601A(F) has no IL maximum; rank C's 1.2 mA is the largest
  listed.
- Lead forming (p.2, Precaution 2): bend at least 2 mm from the body, before
  soldering.

The emitter series resistor, the LED switch and the phototransistor load belong
to the board circuit.

Sourcing: the parts are bought separately (SFH 4550 from ams-OSRAM, TPS601A(F)
from Toshiba) and hand-soldered after the leads are formed, so the component is
excluded from the JLCPCB BOM and placement file (skip_bom). Each fitted sensor
takes one SFH 4550 and one TPS601A(F).
"""

load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Current")

LED_A = io(Net)
LED_K = io(Net)
PT_C = io(Net)
PT_E = io(Net)

Component(
    name="WALL",
    prefix="W",
    symbol=Symbol(library="WallSensor.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("WallSensor_SFH4550_TPS601A_THT.kicad_mod"),
    pins={
        "LED_A": LED_A,
        "LED_K": LED_K,
        "PT_C": PT_C,
        "PT_E": PT_E,
    },
    properties={
        "emitter": "SFH 4550 (ams-OSRAM)",
        "detector": "TPS601A(F) (Toshiba)",
        "assembly": "hand-soldered, leads formed",
        # SFH 4550 v1.8 p.6, OHF05438: TA = 25 C, D <= 0.2, tp <= 150 us.
        "emitter_pulse_current": Current("380mA"),
    },
    skip_bom=True,
)
